WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.010
Matthew tells the birth of
Jesus in five short scenes:

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:09.870
a dream, a star, an escape, a
massacre, and a journey home.

3
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.640
Each scene has an old text, and
again and again a set phrase:

4
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:18.500
this happened so that the
prophet's words might be fulfilled.

5
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.870
But one quote, he will
be called a Nazarene,

6
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.920
matches no verse in the
Old Testament at all.

7
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:29.190
So when Matthew says fulfilled,
what does he actually mean?

8
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.240
In this mission, you'll follow
Matthew's story from Bethlehem to Egypt,

9
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.880
and back to Nazareth.

10
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:40.010
Then you'll set each of his five quotes
beside the words the prophets first wrote.

11
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.620
Your mission: find out what Matthew meant
when he said that the birth fulfilled

12
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.640
the prophets.
